  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $A$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $A$ where every element of $A$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $A$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $A$ and check:\n\n- $p\\in \\{p,s\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $m$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $o\\in \\{t,o\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $q\\in \\{q,r\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $r\\in \\{q,r\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $s\\in \\{p,s\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $t\\in \\{t,o\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $u$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\nThe elements $m$ and $u$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is $\\{m,u\\}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
